A||N||10||merlin||Always defending my Fiero…||||9||
Z||000000||merlin||08-09-2000||10:38 AM||||“Why did you buy that?…”,  “Don’t those cars always break down?…”,  “Why didn’t you get something else like an old Mustang?…”  and the ever so famous…  “Don’t those cars catch fire?…”<P>As of March of this year I am a PROUD owner of a 1987 GT, which was a result of a two year search for a decent example.  However, I find that when I enthusiastically describe my Fiero at parties I often get many puzzling questions that would make you think I just bought a Yugo.  A unique car whose body panels will not rust or dent, where parts are readily and cheaply available sounded like a logical purchase to me.  Don’t get me wrong, my car gets it’s share of looks and I recently read a thread where owners described different times that strangers spoke positively of their cars.  On the flip side though, are there people out there that feel that they are always defending their Fieros?  What is the cause of this negativity?…  The media’s perception of the Fiero during the eighties?…      <BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||Megafiero||08-09-2000||10:52 AM||||merlin,  when I got my Fiero, I was in the same boat.  I was originaly going to get a 69 Chevelle SS, or a 95 Z28, I haden't decieded.  Then to everyone's surprise I got a Fiero.  "WHY DID YOU GET A FIERO!!" was the first thing I heard, and other things a little less kind.  And I was hearing this from my good frinds!!!  Well needless to say aftering giveing them a ride (that took along time, taking them 1 at a time) they realy changed their tune.  "WOW!! I had no idea a Fiero handled like that they said."  Now when we go out on a nice day it seems I always get asked to drive.<P>Also on another note,  I was not allowed to enter my car into a semi local car show once, because my car was a Fiero.  "Your car is not old enough and too stock" they said.  15 years old is not enough, and my car is hardly stock.  Well  when I turned my car around and left,...well when they heard me hammer it they droped they jaws.   Many people tell me my car sounds like it has a SB in it so....<P>No matter how much work it is to defend a Fiero, it is worth it,  I think I can say that for everyone here, or else they probably would not be here.<P>Well better luck to you in the furture, and happy Fiero-ing.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.tir.com/~jcabic/megasig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||08-09-2000||10:57 AM||||Believe me, I know how you feel. When I'm talking about my baby, or Fieros in general, someone will always bring up the fires on early 84 models, they're pices of crap, how they always break down, etc. Instead of getting mad or defensive, I just calmly ask them if they've ever owned a Fiero, or even driven a Fiero. Nine times out of ten the answer is no! <P>Everytime I give someone a ride in a my Fiero, they ALL get out with a big smile on their face! Last time I gave someone a ride in my 88 coupe, she said "where can I get one of these!"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||08-09-2000||11:51 AM||||I just reply "Yep, they do...." and smile. That gets the point across. They all of the sudden become interested in the car.||||reg||1
Z||000004||b lo 0||08-09-2000||12:26 PM||||My mom calls my car my plastic casket<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
Z||000005||elfiero||08-09-2000||03:24 PM||||My favorite thing is when you pull up next<BR>to some ricey thing on the highway they look<BR>at you and smirk.You get ahead of them ,then<BR>hopfully they try and follow you thru a <BR>cloverleaf.You take it at a nice safe 60mph<BR>and look in the rearveiw mirror...you will<BR>notice they are almost always getting their<BR>first glimse of god.LOTS OF FUN!||||reg||12
Z||000006||DRH||08-09-2000||06:22 PM||||I took my Formula (stock V6 5spd) to an autocross Sat. While talking to the guy parked next to me he mentioned a couple of his friends had been refering to my car as 'the car that sounds like a Porshe'. <P>Maybe the perception is improving???<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||08-09-2000||11:11 PM||||Most of the young people I talk to don't know anything about them.  When they see me pull up they look at it, and then they ask "what kind of car is that?" When I say "Fiero" they still don't know what it is!  The older people (30 and up) know about it somewhat, but just the misconceptions (i.e. 84 fiero - fiery crap) thanks to the media.  Being a small car I get the "its a death trap" until I tell them they did better in crash tests then most bigger cars did in 1984.  The coolest thing was in my yellow formula, I just washed it and it was sitting on a lot just before dusk, sort of serene looking at a fiero in the sunset, but anyway these kids about my age walk by and they look at it in amazement.  At first I thought they were going to steal it or something but they just looked at it from every angle.  I VERY proudly walked up to the car and stuck my keys in the door. Then they were like "thos car is soo cool, I have never seen one like it" One kid thought it was a Lotus, the other 2 didn't know what to think.  After some explaining they were very impressed and they gave me their numbers for any that are for sale in the area.  Around here a Honda Civic with 20" Momo's and a loud system gets the most attention, it was nice to see my 100% stock formula get just as much, even if it was for a brief moment in time.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Philphine||08-10-2000||03:32 AM||||some times people ask me about it and i compare it to my chevy. i don't have to worry about rust (appearance wise anyway), 4 wheel independant suspension and disc brakes, and the engine change possibilities. you can kind of see the wheels start turning in their heads.<P>i always say i see alot of fieros in louisville but very few that have much in the way of mods. i don't think people consider the possibilities the car presents as a starting point for something nice. <P>i guess i was hoping after the show more people might look in their driveways and give their fieros more consideration.<BR>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 08-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Homicidal||08-10-2000||04:11 AM||||I get the same.  I guess the hardest thing is telling people they only really caught fire in the 84' models and my car IS an 84!  But I tell them the only reason the car can catch fire is poor owner maitenence.  Besides, look at the new 00' Suv's with their unraveling Firestone tires!!  Our cars weren't the ONLY ones to go through recall.<P>I tell people what I feel:<P>"It's my car.  I paid for it.  I take care of it, and I LOVE it.  I also don't care what others say.  Don't knock it till you've tried it!"<P>And if they are cocky enough to race me, well, usually the last things I hear is:<P>"Are you SURE that's a 4-cylinder?" - My friend after racing his 67' Stang V-8.<P>Besides, after it's all washed and waxed, I don't hear d@mn word!||||reg||1
Z||000010||whamel||08-10-2000||10:58 AM||||Worst part about it is when you call PMCARES and THEY ask you what a Fiero is!!!  'Are you absolutely sure Pontiac made those?'  (I was floored!)||||reg||1
